      { "text": "Magnesium depletion has removed the inhibitory influence of intracellular magnesium on ROMK conductance", "explanation": "Incorrect. Magnesium depletion can aggravate refractory hypokalemia and thiazides do cause magnesium wasting through TRPM6 downregulation, but the primary and immediate mechanism here is increased distal sodium delivery. This would be the correct answer if her hypokalemia had proved resistant to potassium repletion alone." }
